# Medioo site blocks, copied read-only from the box on 2026-10-21 (DR-40, plan task X1); routed per path from W1c.
#
# Source of truth: from W1c on, THIS file. The box's /home/ec2-user/n8n/Caddyfile also holds the n8n ({$DOMAIN}) and
# bddrug (drugdb.eliooo.org) blocks; those are deliberately not copied here, and one reload affects all three tenants.
# The box's medioo/baymax blocks are pasted from this file. Editing this file routes nothing by itself: a path reaches
# medioo-web only once it is routed in the box's Caddyfile (docs/RUNBOOK.md -> Routing a path to medioo-web).
#
# Drift: after every deploy, CI extracts the box's live medioo/baymax blocks (read-only) and compares them with the
# blocks below, comments and blank lines aside (scripts/caddy-drift.sh, tested by scripts/test_caddy_drift.sh). A
# difference fails the deploy job with "box Caddyfile drifted from the repo — fold the box edit in first". Before
# pasting from this file, run the same check by hand; any difference is a box edit to fold in here first, never to
# overwrite.
#
# Editing the box. /home/ec2-user/n8n/Caddyfile is bind-mounted into n8n-caddy-1 as a SINGLE FILE (read-only inside
# the container). Anything that replaces the inode — sed -i, mv of a temp file, rsync, an editor that saves by
# rename — leaves the container reading the old file, and `caddy reload` then quietly reloads the stale config.
#   cd /home/ec2-user/n8n
#   cp Caddyfile Caddyfile.bak-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M)
#   cat /path/to/new-Caddyfile > Caddyfile                     # in place only; never sed -i, mv or rsync
#   docker exec n8n-caddy-1 cat /etc/caddy/Caddyfile | diff - Caddyfile          # must print nothing
#   docker exec n8n-caddy-1 caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile        # must say Valid configuration
#   docker exec n8n-caddy-1 caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#   curl -sI https://medioo.eliooo.org/ ; curl -sI https://drugdb.eliooo.org/ ; curl -sI https://<n8n host>/
#     -> compare each status code with the one recorded before the edit; any change means restore the backup
#        (cat Caddyfile.bak-... > Caddyfile) and reload.
#
# Headers: deleting `-Server` makes Caddy defer this header block to response-write time, so the values below
# OVERWRITE whatever the upstream sends. Caddy is therefore the owner of HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options and
# Referrer-Policy on every path, Java's or Next's; an upstream that sets a different Referrer-Policy is overruled.
#
# DR-40 A1: Java is the default. A path goes to medioo-web:3000 only once it is listed here and applied on the box.
# Flipping a route back is a one-line edit plus the procedure above, and the routes floor (RUNBOOK -> Rollback).
# The handle blocks are mutually exclusive: the most specific path matcher wins, and the bare `handle` is Java. Only
# /app/healthz is routed so far (W1c); /_next/* and /fonts/* come with the first HTML route.
#
# Referrer-Policy stays strict-origin-when-cross-origin, the value production has sent since before the rebuild
# (noted for the PO in the W1c PR): medioo-web's own headers send the same value, and Caddy overwrites it anyway.

medioo.eliooo.org {
	encode zstd gzip

	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		-Server
	}

	handle /app/healthz {
		reverse_proxy medioo-web:3000
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy medscribe-ai:8086
	}
}

# Old public name (DR-15, 2026-09-19): every URL already sent to families keeps working via a permanent redirect.
baymax.eliooo.org {
	redir https://medioo.eliooo.org{uri} permanent
}
